from h import *
A = dict(id="A", levels=L1, kind="Web page", source="Wanderwise Tours website", title="Dead Sea day trip", body=[
 {"p": "Float in the famous Dead Sea on a relaxed day out from Tel Aviv. Our friendly guide will tell you all about the area on the journey."},
 {"h": "What is included"},
 {"p": "A minibus, towels, a picnic lunch and entry to the beach."},
 {"h": "Times"},
 {"p": "We leave at 8:00 am and return at 5:00 pm. Please be at the meeting point ten minutes early."},
 {"h": "What to bring"},
 {"p": "Sun cream, a hat and sandals that you can wear in the water."},
 {"h": "Price"},
 {"p": "Adults £45. Children under 14 £30."}])
B = dict(id="B", levels=L1, kind="Magazine article", source="Wanderwise Tours travel magazine", title="Floating in the Dead Sea: what to expect", body=[
 {"p": "The Dead Sea is one of the most unusual places in the world. It sits more than 400 metres below sea level, which makes it the lowest place on land on Earth, and its water is so salty that it holds your body up. Even people who cannot swim can lie back and float."},
 {"h": "How to get the most from your visit"},
 {"p": "Local guide Noa Levi has taken hundreds of visitors to the Dead Sea, and she has some simple advice. \"Walk in slowly, sit down in the water and then lean back,\" she says. \"Never put your head under, and keep splashing to a minimum. Salt water in the eyes really stings.\""},
 {"p": "Salt water also stings tiny cuts, so avoid shaving on the morning of your visit. Most people stay in the water for a short time (about 15 minutes is enough), because the salt can dry out your skin. Afterwards, rinse off in the fresh water showers on the beach, which also has changing rooms nearby."},
 {"h": "Mud and minerals"},
 {"p": "Many visitors cover themselves in the dark mud from the shore. The mud is full of minerals, and it makes your skin feel wonderfully soft. Let it dry for a few minutes in the sun, then wash it off in the sea. Do not forget to take a camera, but keep it somewhere dry!"},
 {"h": "Sun and water"},
 {"p": "It can be extremely hot by the Dead Sea, even in the early morning. Wear a hat, put on plenty of sun cream and drink lots of fresh water. Wear sandals, too, because the stones on the shore can be sharp. Children should always stay close to an adult in the water."},
 {"p": "Floating there is the most relaxing thing you can do on holiday, and it is an experience you will never forget."}])
C = dict(id="C", levels=L1, kind="Forum post", source="Travel Talk forum, thread: \"Is the Dead Sea day trip worth it?\"", title="Re: Is the Dead Sea day trip worth it?", body=[
 {"p": "Hi! I went last spring with two friends and I'd say yes, it's worth it, but go early. The guide on our minibus was lovely and told us loads about the desert on the way, which made the long journey go quickly."},
 {"p": "Floating was the weirdest and funniest thing I've ever done. You just lie back and the water holds you up, no effort at all! We took loads of photos of each other reading the paper, which I know everyone does."},
 {"p": "The not-so-great bits: the beach was packed by 11 o'clock and it was boiling. I splashed water in my eye and it stung like mad, so listen when they tell you not to put your head under. The salt also dries on your skin and feels sticky, so use the showers. The picnic lunch was a bit boring too: just a cheese sandwich and an apple. Overall though, I'd go again in a heartbeat."},
 {"p": "My tips:"},
 {"ul": ["Go as early as you can.", "Take a bottle of fresh water to drink and to rinse your face.", "Wear sandals, because the stones are sharp.", "Don't forget sun cream."]},
 {"p": "Hope that helps. Has anyone else been?"}])

